@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# Local-only voice correlation experiment
+
+This is not a production implementation or an authenticated API. The patch to
+Evolution adds an internal optional reserved ID for direct audio; it adds no
+HTTP endpoint. The PoC ledger and authority callbacks are synthetic. Never
+connect them to a real customer, provider, production database or credentials.
+
+The internal correlated path is **unconditionally disabled** and refuses before
+route lookup or conversion for every runtime and environment. The former
+opt-in and three-file rc13 check have been removed: rc13 is not an approved
+production dependency. A signature-verification issue independently reproduced
+in both rc9 and rc13 remains unresolved. Existing calls without the internal
+correlation argument do not invoke this guard. Replacing the denial requires a
+separately accepted security fix and review; see `deployment-and-rollback.md`.
+
+The disposable PostgreSQL ledger persists a fingerprint and a Baileys-generated
+ID before an atomic one-shot claim. Unknown outcomes remain claimed; no timer,
+retry or cancellation reopens them. The bridge extracts the modified Evolution
+methods and sends synthetic bytes to actual Baileys 7.0.0-rc.9 until an
+intercepted fake `sendNode`. Audio media is replaced by a synthetic cache hit;
+this does not test upload, encryption, WhatsApp delivery or real webhooks.
+
+`VOICE_POC_ADMIN_URL=postgresql://...localhost.../postgres node --test poc-tests/protocol-postgres.test.mjs`
+requires a disposable local PostgreSQL; it creates and drops a random dedicated
+database. `node --test poc-tests/evolution-bridge.test.cjs` exercises the bridge.
+Both tests have local third-party dependencies and require a compatible Node 24.
+No credentials or persistent database settings are supplied by this project.
+
+`node --test poc-tests/runtime-guard.test.cjs poc-tests/evolution-bridge.test.cjs`
+checks that the actual guard rejects both locally identified package copies,
+missing packages and every tested legacy opt-in. The guard does not resolve or
+verify package bytes: it always rejects. The test bridge extracts TypeScript
+methods and mocks Evolution and the provider; its no-op guard is an explicit
+synthetic-only bypass outside the service. It is not a complete Evolution
+process or image test. Tests require the local TypeScript dependency in the
+Connect checkout.
+The tests can be run with `--network none`, read-only input mounts and
+a temporary writable `/tmp`, using the already available `postgres:16` image
+only as a filesystem (its database server was not started):
+
+```sh
+docker --host=unix:///var/run/docker.sock run --rm --pull=never --network none \
+  --read-only --cap-drop ALL --security-opt no-new-privileges --user 1000:1000 \
+  --pids-limit 128 --memory 512m --tmpfs /tmp:rw,noexec,nosuid,size=128m \
+  --mount type=bind,src=/workspace/voice-evolution-runtime-patch,dst=/work,readonly \
+  --mount type=bind,src=/workspace/voice-beintaskbot-connect/node_modules/typescript,dst=/workspace/voice-beintaskbot-connect/node_modules/typescript,readonly \
+  --mount type=bind,src=/workspace/voice-poc-deps,dst=/workspace/voice-poc-deps,readonly \
+  --mount type=bind,src=/workspace/voice-security-poc/rc13,dst=/workspace/voice-security-poc/rc13,readonly \
+  --mount type=bind,src=/opt/codex/runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin/node,dst=/test-node,readonly \
+  --entrypoint /test-node postgres:16 --test /work/poc-tests/runtime-guard.test.cjs /work/poc-tests/evolution-bridge.test.cjs
+```
+
+Security limits that block production use:
+
+* Synthetic event field equality is not proof of event origin or author.
+  The deployed pinned Baileys rc9 is affected by GHSA-qvv5-jq5g-4cgg; upgraded
+  Evolution compatibility and event authenticity require separate review.
+  See https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys/security/advisories/GHSA-qvv5-jq5g-4cgg
+  and `security-neutral/`. Matching dependency bytes and neutral fixtures do not
+  demonstrate production exploitation or verify that rc13 is compatible.
+* Synthetic identity and permission callbacks do not implement authentication,
+  tenant isolation or revocation; dispatch is not atomically bound to a verified
+  real socket generation. Route lookup and account rotation require integration.
+* A single local ledger is tested, not distributed Worker/Connect/Evolution
+  storage or endpoint failure boundaries. `claimed` means only that the local
+  intent was claimed; it does not prove dispatch began. The separate process
+  exits at relay entry, before provider send. A new request ID is a new intent.
+* The test disables Evolution's optional OpenAI transcription side effect;
+  real instance configuration and existing consent/cost policy require review.
+  The receipt is extracted from Evolution's locally mocked `prepareMessage`,
+  not an observed production response.
+* Direct-message only. Groups are explicitly rejected. The existing held PRs'
+  persistent channel-wide AI pause is not fixed by this experiment.
+* The optional third-repository Evolution patch has not passed a complete build,
+  service integration, security review or real-provider test and must not be
+  deployed automatically. No production changes have been made.
