+# Baileys self-only guard: isolated neutral comparison
+
+This local experiment compares pinned Baileys `7.0.0-rc.9` and `7.0.0-rc13`.
+The rc9 `node_modules` is a local copy of the previously installed package;
+rc13 was installed from npm with lifecycle scripts disabled. Verify the
+versions and SHA-256 values printed by the test against your own supply-chain
+records before using the result.
+
+The fixtures contain only synthetic message keys and empty protocol data. No
+embedded messages, real contacts, auth state, provider sessions or keys are
+used. History processing is disabled. Event emitter, resend cache, signal
+repository and key store are fakes; writes and unexpected transactions throw.
+The test invokes the actual installed `processMessage` implementation.
+
+Run with a separately installed Node 24 binary inside a locally available
+Debian-compatible image. The example below uses an existing `postgres:16`
+image only as a filesystem; its database entrypoint is not started. Nothing is
+pulled, and the entire experiment directory and Node binary are mounted
+read-only. Change the Node path if necessary.
+
+```sh
+docker --host=unix:///var/run/docker.sock run --rm --pull=never \
+  --network none --read-only --cap-drop ALL --security-opt no-new-privileges \
+  --user 1000:1000 --pids-limit 128 --memory 512m \
+  --mount type=bind,src=/workspace/voice-security-poc,dst=/work,readonly \
+  --mount type=bind,src=/opt/codex/runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin/node,dst=/test-node,readonly \
+  --entrypoint /test-node postgres:16 /work/test-neutral.mjs
+```
+
+It checks the difference in local dispatch for four inert self-only protocol
+types and checks the continuing handling of several ordinary cross-user
+protocol types. `GROUP_MEMBER_LABEL_CHANGE` is checked only for rc13 because
+the copied rc9 implementation has no corresponding branch. It does not
+exercise real history synchronization, decrypt a message, create a spoofed
+message, open a WhatsApp connection, or demonstrate production exploitability.
+The input `fromMe` flag is supplied by the test; this does not exercise
+`messages-recv`, authenticate the sender or validate rc13's real-device
+`fromMe` parsing fix. Empty peer-response data does not exercise placeholder
+resend or webhook propagation.
+It is not a full security audit or proof that Evolution 2.3.7 is compatible
+with rc13, nor proof that any actual image runs these copies. Real message
+delivery and coexistence behaviour remain untested.
